<div class="modal-content">
  <div class="modal-header">
    <button class="modal-close" @click="$refs.helpDialog.close()" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h2>Quick Reference</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="modal-body">

  <p>Please see our
    <a href="http://kanjialive.com/user-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="User Guide (opens in new tab)">User Guide</a> for detailed explanations of all of <em>Kanji alive's</em> features or watch our
    <a href="http://www.youtube.com/kanjialive/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="short demonstration videos (opens in new tab)">short demonstration videos</a>. If you are having technical difficulties, please refer to our
    <a href="http://kanjialive.com/troubleshooting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Troubleshooting (opens in new tab)">Troubleshooting</a> page.
  </p>
  <p lang="ja">詳細は、メーニューの「日本語」内にある使用説明とトラブルシューティングをご参照ください。</p>

  <h3>Quick Search</h3>
  <p>
    Enter a <em>single</em> search term for kanji from one of the following four categories: 1) a kanji character, 2) an Onyomi reading in katakana, 3) a Kunyomi reading in hiragana, 4) a kanji's simplified English meaning.
  </p>
  <p>Examples:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>親</li>
    <li>シン</li>
    <li>おや</li>
    <li>parent</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Note: In Quick Search mode Onyomi and Kunyomi readings may only be entered in Japanese. Please use the Advanced Search mode to search for kanji by reading in romaji.
  </p>

  <h3>Advanced Search</h3>
  <p>
    Enter one or more search terms in Japanese or romaji from all of the available categories in <em>Kanji alive</em>. Advanced search queries <em>must</em> be entered in the form
    <kbd>key:value</kbd> where <em>key</em> refers to the search category (e.g. Onyomi reading) and <em>value</em> refers to the search term for a given key (for example,
    <kbd>on:shin</kbd> or
    <kbd>on:シン</kbd>).
  </p>
  <p><strong>List of available Keys:</strong></p>
  <table class="help-table">
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>on:</kbd></th>
      <td>Onyomi reading, R/J (Katakana)</td>
      <td><kbd>on:shin</kbd> or <kbd>on:シン</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>kun:</kbd></th>
      <td>Kunyomi reading, R/J (Hiragana)</td>
      <td><kbd>kun:oya</kbd> or <kbd>kun:おや</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>kem:</kbd></th>
      <td>Kanji English meaning, E</td>
      <td><kbd>kem:parent</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>ks:</kbd></th>
      <td>Kanji stroke number, #</td>
      <td><kbd>ks:16</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>kanji:</kbd></th>
      <td>Kanji character, J</td>
      <td><kbd>kanji:親</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>rjn:</kbd></th>
      <td>Radical Japanese name, R/J (Hiragana)</td>
      <td><kbd>rjn:miru</kbd> or <kbd>rjn:みる</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>rem:</kbd></th>
      <td>Radical English meaning, E</td>
      <td><kbd>rem:see</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>rs:</kbd></th>
      <td>Radical stroke number, #</td>
      <td><kbd>rs:7</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>rpos:</kbd></th>
      <td>Radical Position, R/J (Hiragana)</td>
      <td><kbd>rpos:hen</kbd> or <kbd>rpos:へん</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>grade:</kbd></th>
      <td>Grade level, #</td>
      <td><kbd>grade:2</kbd></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>text:</kbd></th>
      <td>Textbook</td>
      <td>see below for details</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><kbd>list:</kbd></th>
      <td>Study List</td>
      <td>see below for details</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <p>
    In Advanced Search mode, two or more search terms may be combined by entering these one after the other separated by a space. The search results will show only those kanji common to all of the categories listed (for example,
    <kbd>grade:3 rjn:ninben</kbd> – all Grade 3 kanji with the radical "ninben"). Any number of search categories may be combined in this manner.
  </p>

