  </table>
  <p>
    Note: Although it is possible to enter only the name of a textbook or study list after the
    <kbd>text:</kbd> or
    <kbd>list:</kbd> key (e.g.
    <kbd>text:cij</kbd> or
    <kbd>list:ap</kbd>), this would show <em>all</em> kanji found in the respective resource. For this reason, it is usually helpful to append a volume and/or lesson number to limit your search (e.g.
    <kbd>text:cij:c6</kbd> or
    <kbd>list:ap:c3</kbd>).
  </p>
  <p>
    Please refer to <a href="http://kanjialive.com/supported-textbooks/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Supported Textbooks and Study Lists (opens in new tab)">Supported Textbooks and Study Lists</a> on our website for additional details on the division of textbooks into volumes and/or chapters/lessons as well as textbook kanji not supported by <em>Kanji alive</em>.
  </p>

  <p><strong>List of available Values for Study Lists:</strong></p>
  <table class="help-table">
    <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>ap:</kbd></th><td>Advanced Placement Exam</td><td><kbd>list:ap:c3</kbd></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>mac:</kbd></th><td>Macquarie University</td><td><kbd>list:mac:c12</kbd></td></tr>
  </table>

  <h3>Search Results</h3>
  <p>All kanji search results are initially shown in a single block, sorted by kanji stroke number. Two additional sort modes are available for viewing kanji, grouped together either by radical stroke number or kanji stroke number. In these two modes all kanji in a group are further sorted by the canonical order of their Japanese radicals. In the results, the radicals are shown in grey and in a smaller type size to the left of their respective kanji.</p>

  <h3>Navigation</h3>
  <table class="help-table">
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Sort modes</th>
      <td>Click on the "Sort" icon in the navigation bar or use the <kbd>&uarr;</kbd> and <kbd>&darr;</kbd> arrow keys to switch sort modes</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Page results</th>
      <td>Click on the pointed brackets to the left and right of the "Sort" icon, drag the horizontal scrollbar or use the <kbd>&larr;</kbd> and <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> arrow keys to view additional pages of results</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">View kanji details</th>
      <td>Click on a kanji to view its details</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  </div>
</div>
